1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,929
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:23,199 --> 00:00:25,451
Previously on Dating Alys Perez.

3
00:00:28,162 --> 00:00:30,207
705 emails.

4
00:00:30,915 --> 00:00:33,126
That madman hasn't stopped.

5
00:00:34,961 --> 00:00:36,087
How are you?

6
00:00:36,879 --> 00:00:38,423
We're doing fine here.

7
00:00:38,715 --> 00:00:40,341
Wake up, please?

8
00:00:41,134 --> 00:00:44,345
I made a tiny altar in memory of Marco.

9
00:00:45,346 --> 00:00:46,681
Hello, Marco.

10
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:49,308
They told me, “Give up, Drake.”

11
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,019
“She's moved on.”

12
00:00:51,519 --> 00:00:52,770
But hell, I won't.

13
00:00:53,563 --> 00:00:57,692
[singing] Happy birthday, happy birthday.

14
00:00:58,026 --> 00:01:00,069
You said you love me.

15
00:01:00,445 --> 00:01:02,238
I'm holding you to that, Alys.

16
00:01:02,905 --> 00:01:04,824
He could hear, he could feel.

17
00:01:05,116 --> 00:01:08,119
We were surprised that he finally woke up now.

18
00:01:31,017 --> 00:01:32,143
Gabby, I'm off.

19
00:01:36,272 --> 00:01:37,106
Bye, Tommy.

20
00:01:37,273 --> 00:01:38,941
Hey, are you going to see him again?

21
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:39,859
Mhm!

22
00:01:40,026 --> 00:01:40,818
Bye, Kevs!

23
00:01:41,569 --> 00:01:42,361
Bye.

24
00:01:43,029 --> 00:01:44,113
Where do you live again?

25
00:01:44,113 --> 00:01:45,114
Pampanga.

26
00:01:45,114 --> 00:01:46,991
Right, Pampanga.

27
00:01:48,076 --> 00:01:49,410
What's your favorite food?

28
00:01:49,827 --> 00:01:50,703
Adobo.

29
00:01:51,037 --> 00:01:51,913
Really?

30
00:01:51,913 --> 00:01:52,789
Adobo?

31
00:01:53,956 --> 00:01:56,417
It has been months since you woke up.

32
00:01:56,626 --> 00:01:57,835
And...

33
00:01:57,835 --> 00:01:59,003
you seem okay.

34
00:02:00,171 --> 00:02:02,632
I'm just happy to see you okay.

35
00:02:03,257 --> 00:02:04,759
That you're living your life.

36
00:02:06,302 --> 00:02:07,470
Without me.

37
00:02:15,728 --> 00:02:18,481
But I’m still scared to approach you.

38
00:02:21,359 --> 00:02:22,680
I don't know

39
00:02:23,152 --> 00:02:26,781
how you'll react if we ever meet again.

40
00:02:28,658 --> 00:02:32,286
I don't know if you'll let me back into your life.

41
00:02:33,579 --> 00:02:34,580
So...

42
00:02:35,081 --> 00:02:38,626
that's why I'm happy watching you from afar.

43
00:03:00,982 --> 00:03:02,567
I promised myself,

44
00:03:03,151 --> 00:03:06,279
I’d only come back to the Philippines when you wake up.

45
00:03:07,655 --> 00:03:09,073
But I don't know.

46
00:03:10,575 --> 00:03:14,287
There's still a hole in my heart that I need to fill.

47
00:05:16,075 --> 00:05:17,159
- Miss. - Hello!

48
00:05:17,285 --> 00:05:19,578
- Excuse me. - Here's your Newyork cheesecake.

49
00:05:20,246 --> 00:05:22,957
Your iced latte.

50
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:25,334
And for you, sir...

51
00:05:25,751 --> 00:05:27,878
Your hot double shot americano.

52
00:05:27,878 --> 00:05:30,381
- Enjoy! - God, service is so slow.

53
00:05:31,716 --> 00:05:32,508
Yes, sir?

54
00:05:32,508 --> 00:05:33,676
How may I help you?

55
00:05:40,891 --> 00:05:42,268
Everything cool, Alys?

56
00:05:46,314 --> 00:05:47,440
Tripp?

57
00:05:47,982 --> 00:05:48,649
Hey.

58
00:05:49,942 --> 00:05:50,609
Zy!

59
00:05:52,111 --> 00:05:53,612
You can move.

60
00:05:56,324 --> 00:05:57,199
How about a coffee?

61
00:06:00,202 --> 00:06:00,870
You know what, Zy?

62
00:06:01,412 --> 00:06:03,122
I’ve been sleeping in the hospital for three years.

63
00:06:03,497 --> 00:06:04,874
You're still as slow as ever.

64
00:06:04,874 --> 00:06:05,745
What's wrong with you?

65
00:06:19,597 --> 00:06:20,681
I've been looking for you.

66
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:24,143
Tofer told me that you worked here.

67
00:06:24,977 --> 00:06:26,395
So, I came to see you.

68
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:30,107
Aren't you mad at me?

69
00:06:35,029 --> 00:06:36,405
Can I still do something about it?

70
00:06:38,491 --> 00:06:39,667
I’m sorry.

71
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:41,744
Zy...

72
00:06:43,829 --> 00:06:44,747
Zy!

73
00:06:45,748 --> 00:06:47,097
I'm doing fine.

74
00:06:48,209 --> 00:06:49,886
Don't worry, okay?

75
00:06:52,755 --> 00:06:55,299
It’s enough for me that the years you’ve lost

76
00:06:55,299 --> 00:06:56,467
were meant to watch over me.

77
00:06:57,927 --> 00:06:58,844
Thank you.

78
00:07:01,097 --> 00:07:03,015
It's the least that I can do.

79
00:07:04,862 --> 00:07:06,018
Alys...

80
00:07:07,144 --> 00:07:08,354
You're free now.

81
00:07:10,606 --> 00:07:12,612
Do whatever you want to do.

82
00:07:15,111 --> 00:07:17,446
I know in my heart that

83
00:07:17,446 --> 00:07:19,073
I held you for so long.

84
00:07:20,550 --> 00:07:21,867
Because I love you.

85
00:07:23,828 --> 00:07:26,497
But I know who truly makes you happy.

86
00:07:27,623 --> 00:07:28,332
So, go.

87
00:07:29,875 --> 00:07:30,709
Go back to Drake.

88
00:07:32,837 --> 00:07:34,081
Don't wait for me.

89
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:35,631
Huh?

90
00:07:35,631 --> 00:07:36,382
But...

91
00:07:42,638 --> 00:07:43,597
Zy!

92
00:07:46,267 --> 00:07:47,726
You did nothing wrong.

93
00:07:48,819 --> 00:07:50,445
I have never blamed you.

94
00:07:50,938 --> 00:07:51,897
I am not blaming you.

95
00:07:52,481 --> 00:07:53,941
I will never blame you.

96
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:57,699
Remember what I told you?

97
00:07:58,863 --> 00:08:00,364
You should always be happy, right?

98
00:08:01,991 --> 00:08:02,950
Do you remember?

99
00:08:05,911 --> 00:08:06,704
Okay?

100
00:08:07,204 --> 00:08:08,205
Good.

101
00:08:09,457 --> 00:08:10,666
Don't be stubborn.

102
00:08:11,292 --> 00:08:12,411
Go back to Drake.

103
00:08:14,712 --> 00:08:16,088
I’m okay now.

104
00:08:17,256 --> 00:08:18,632
Go back inside.

105
00:08:19,133 --> 00:08:20,301
I've taken up enough of your time.

106
00:08:20,301 --> 00:08:21,385
No, no!

107
00:08:21,385 --> 00:08:22,470
Tripp!

108
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:25,014
You can talk as much as you want.

109
00:08:25,306 --> 00:08:27,099
You can talk the entire day!

110
00:08:27,099 --> 00:08:27,808
That's okay!

111
00:08:27,808 --> 00:08:29,101
I don’t mind.

112
00:08:29,685 --> 00:08:31,854
As long as I have proof that you’re alive.

113
00:08:32,354 --> 00:08:33,522
You're breathing.

114
00:08:33,856 --> 00:08:36,484
You’re talking. You’re smiling.

115
00:08:38,068 --> 00:08:40,247
Tell me anything.

116
00:08:41,655 --> 00:08:42,948
I’m contented with that.

117
00:08:49,371 --> 00:08:50,357
I'm real.

118
00:08:51,415 --> 00:08:52,505
You believe me now?

119
00:08:58,621 --> 00:08:59,681
By the way,

120
00:09:00,549 --> 00:09:02,146
my mom told me that

121
00:09:02,593 --> 00:09:04,553
you'd only go back to the Philippines when I get better.

122
00:09:06,889 --> 00:09:07,973
Start packing, okay?

123
00:09:08,051 --> 00:09:09,511
- Alright, bye. - Damn it, Tripp!

124
00:09:09,615 --> 00:09:10,458
Ouch!

125
00:09:10,726 --> 00:09:11,310
Come on!

126
00:09:11,435 --> 00:09:13,208
You still have the nerve to joke around?

127
00:09:13,437 --> 00:09:14,897
Do you want to send me back to the hospital?

128
00:09:15,356 --> 00:09:15,898
Sorry.

129
00:09:15,898 --> 00:09:17,024
You really seem mad at me.

130
00:09:17,233 --> 00:09:18,239
Sorry.

131
00:09:21,946 --> 00:09:22,821
By the way,

132
00:09:26,951 --> 00:09:28,239
I'm going back to New York.

133
00:09:30,246 --> 00:09:31,247
My flight’s tonight.

134
00:09:33,222 --> 00:09:35,516
I just came to say goodbye.

135
00:09:35,884 --> 00:09:37,724
What about your job here?

136
00:09:40,798 --> 00:09:41,924
Have you been stalking me?

137
00:09:47,445 --> 00:09:48,373
Anyway,

138
00:09:48,681 --> 00:09:50,933
I'll be going.

139
00:09:53,394 --> 00:09:55,437
Don't you want to try our coffee?

140
00:09:55,997 --> 00:09:58,041
Just for a bit. Come on!

141
00:10:31,974 --> 00:10:32,975
Go on, Silly.

142
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:34,393
They're looking for you already.

143
00:10:34,643 --> 00:10:36,228
Your customers might get mad.

144
00:11:20,856 --> 00:11:23,870
But I know who truly makes you happy.

145
00:11:24,693 --> 00:11:25,569
So, go.

146
00:11:26,862 --> 00:11:28,096
Go back to Drake.

147
00:11:32,076 --> 00:11:34,536
I hope he hasn't changed his number yet.

148
00:11:42,336 --> 00:11:43,712
Alys...

149
00:11:44,963 --> 00:11:46,031
Drake?

150
00:11:47,675 --> 00:11:49,510
I’ve waited for years.

151
00:11:50,346 --> 00:11:52,156
Tripp said it himself.

152
00:11:52,930 --> 00:11:56,225
I should go back to the one who truly makes me happy.

153
00:11:58,123 --> 00:11:59,082
I'm coming home.

154
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,271
To you.

155
00:12:02,272 --> 00:12:04,233
Turn around.

156
00:12:24,878 --> 00:12:26,964
Aren’t you going to hug me?

157
00:12:32,970 --> 00:12:35,931
I freaking love you, Drake Sebastian Palma!

158
00:12:36,181 --> 00:12:39,393
I thought it would go away after all the pain that you've caused me.

159
00:12:39,393 --> 00:12:41,395
But the more I distance myself from you,

160
00:12:41,395 --> 00:12:43,439
the more I find myself looking for you.

161
00:12:43,647 --> 00:12:44,857
I freaking love you.

162
00:12:46,483 --> 00:12:47,609
Bad words.

163
00:12:49,319 --> 00:12:50,404
I freaking love you!

164
00:12:50,529 --> 00:12:52,781
I freaking, freaking, freaking love you!

165
00:12:56,118 --> 00:12:56,910
Okay.

166
00:12:57,995 --> 00:12:58,912
I get it.

167
00:12:59,455 --> 00:13:00,973
I believe you.

168
00:13:19,284 --> 00:13:22,349
I love you to the moon and back.

169
00:13:24,563 --> 00:13:26,064
Marry me.

170
00:13:27,858 --> 00:13:29,860
But this time,

171
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:32,738
I want to do it in front of God,

172
00:13:34,031 --> 00:13:37,034
and the people we love.

173
00:13:38,702 --> 00:13:40,996
I want to see you walk the aisle

174
00:13:41,747 --> 00:13:44,208
while I wait for you at the end.

175
00:13:46,210 --> 00:13:48,879
It feels so good to hear that, Drake.

176
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:52,508
After everything that happened in our story,

177
00:13:55,636 --> 00:13:58,680
you’re still the one I’ll come home to.

178
00:14:01,433 --> 00:14:03,268
So, is that a yes?

179
00:14:04,353 --> 00:14:05,896
A yes to what?

180
00:14:07,272 --> 00:14:08,690
To forever.

181
00:14:09,191 --> 00:14:10,609
With me.

182
00:14:15,864 --> 00:14:16,907
Yes, Drake.

183
00:14:18,826 --> 00:14:20,452
To the moon and back.

184
00:14:22,955 --> 00:14:24,373
But...

185
00:14:24,998 --> 00:14:26,166
But what?

186
00:14:28,252 --> 00:14:30,796
But this time, we need to do it right.

187
00:14:32,881 --> 00:14:34,424
No one will get hurt anymore.

188
00:14:34,967 --> 00:14:37,094
No more dragging anyone else into this.

189
00:14:38,353 --> 00:14:40,504
I think we all deserve to be happy.

190
00:14:43,976 --> 00:14:45,227
Alys...

191
00:14:51,250 --> 00:14:52,569
Can you be mine?

192
00:14:52,901 --> 00:14:53,917
Again?

193
00:14:54,236 --> 00:14:55,120
Please?

194
00:16:43,428 --> 00:16:44,721
Hey.

195
00:16:45,138 --> 00:16:47,099
Why do you look like you’re about to be executed?

196
00:16:49,977 --> 00:16:50,936
I'm just kidding.

197
00:16:52,604 --> 00:16:53,897
I’m just trying to make you guys laugh.

198
00:16:54,815 --> 00:16:55,732
You look so serious.

199
00:16:57,067 --> 00:16:58,026
So, now what?

200
00:16:58,610 --> 00:16:59,695
This is it?

201
00:17:00,153 --> 00:17:01,571
We just stare at each other all day?

202
00:17:02,698 --> 00:17:04,408
- Sorry. - Sorry.

203
00:17:05,617 --> 00:17:06,535
Wow.

204
00:17:07,536 --> 00:17:09,099
You even answer at the same time now!

205
00:17:13,208 --> 00:17:14,376
But, seriously.

206
00:17:15,877 --> 00:17:16,837
Sorry for what?

207
00:17:17,295 --> 00:17:18,797
- For everything. - For everything.

208
00:17:22,342 --> 00:17:23,468
You know what?

209
00:17:24,011 --> 00:17:25,095
You guys look stupid.

210
00:17:25,387 --> 00:17:26,471
Don’t you know that?

211
00:17:33,103 --> 00:17:35,480
Do you believe in the saying,

212
00:17:36,314 --> 00:17:38,567
“Everything happens for a reason”?

213
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:43,905
Because for me, I do.

214
00:17:44,698 --> 00:17:48,201
I don’t know if I’m just saying that to make myself feel better

215
00:17:48,201 --> 00:17:49,911
about what happened to me.

216
00:17:50,579 --> 00:17:52,622
About what happened to all of us.

217
00:17:53,665 --> 00:17:55,333
But I believe that...

218
00:17:56,168 --> 00:17:57,961
everything happens for a reason.

219
00:18:01,673 --> 00:18:03,300
I believe that...

220
00:18:04,885 --> 00:18:07,929
I’m not just some insignificant part of all this.

221
00:18:09,556 --> 00:18:12,350
That I was put in your story...

222
00:18:13,810 --> 00:18:16,313
so that we could all get to this point.

223
00:18:17,022 --> 00:18:18,065
To the ending where,

224
00:18:18,690 --> 00:18:19,733
finally,

225
00:18:20,650 --> 00:18:24,279
you both know for certain that you’re meant to be together.

226
00:18:25,864 --> 00:18:27,973
That’s why you should never apologize to me.

227
00:18:30,243 --> 00:18:31,981
It happened because it had to.

228
00:18:33,747 --> 00:18:35,248
I don't regret anything.

229
00:18:40,644 --> 00:18:42,019
To be honest,

230
00:18:45,759 --> 00:18:47,411
I'm the one who should be sorry.

231
00:18:51,681 --> 00:18:52,933
Drake...

232
00:18:54,309 --> 00:18:55,519
You were right.

233
00:18:56,895 --> 00:18:59,231
Somehow, someway,

234
00:19:01,274 --> 00:19:04,069
I was the reason why you two broke up.

235
00:19:06,822 --> 00:19:08,115
To be fair,

236
00:19:09,574 --> 00:19:11,368
I was really concerned for you.

237
00:19:12,035 --> 00:19:14,996
And aside from the fact that...

238
00:19:15,455 --> 00:19:16,706
I loved you.

239
00:19:18,917 --> 00:19:20,252
But, it didn't work out.

240
00:19:24,548 --> 00:19:25,924
But I'll admit it.

241
00:19:27,843 --> 00:19:30,095
I just hated the idea that...

242
00:19:30,554 --> 00:19:32,472
you'd win again.

243
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:34,599
You’ll get ahead of me again.

244
00:19:36,434 --> 00:19:38,186
That you’ll be the one chosen again.

245
00:19:41,565 --> 00:19:43,692
Remember what I told you?

246
00:19:44,109 --> 00:19:45,527
That you were ruining Alys.

247
00:19:48,155 --> 00:19:49,114
And I'm sorry.

248
00:19:51,032 --> 00:19:52,617
Things went spiral from there.

249
00:19:55,203 --> 00:19:57,414
You know, after everything that happened to me...

250
00:19:58,373 --> 00:19:59,207
The accident.

251
00:20:02,085 --> 00:20:03,378
That was my karma.

252
00:20:06,548 --> 00:20:07,966
I deserved it.

253
00:20:10,635 --> 00:20:11,428
Drake.

254
00:20:20,687 --> 00:20:21,688
Take care of Alys, okay?

255
00:20:25,650 --> 00:20:26,484
Alys.

256
00:20:28,695 --> 00:20:29,821
Be happy.

257
00:20:32,032 --> 00:20:32,782
Please.

258
00:20:37,037 --> 00:20:38,371
Alys, did you not hear what I said?

259
00:20:39,206 --> 00:20:41,458
Come on, you’ve been crying all the way to the end.

260
00:20:41,458 --> 00:20:42,667
Seriously, enough already.

261
00:20:46,588 --> 00:20:47,214
So?

262
00:20:48,089 --> 00:20:49,174
I guess, that’s it.

263
00:20:49,758 --> 00:20:50,800
I'll go ahead.

264
00:20:52,052 --> 00:20:53,511
I've been asleep for three years.

265
00:20:53,929 --> 00:20:55,222
I've got a lot to catch up on.

266
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,849
See you in the Philippines?

267
00:21:09,611 --> 00:21:10,415
Tripp!

268
00:21:19,204 --> 00:21:21,248
Uh, guys.

269
00:21:21,790 --> 00:21:22,832
This is Amber.

270
00:21:23,354 --> 00:21:24,147
My friend.

271
00:21:25,252 --> 00:21:27,629
Amber, this is Drake, Alys.

272
00:21:27,629 --> 00:21:29,297
Alys, Drake, Amber.

273
00:21:31,258 --> 00:21:32,259
Hello, Amber.

274
00:21:32,467 --> 00:21:33,218
Hi, Amber.

275
00:21:33,385 --> 00:21:34,177
Hi, guys.

276
00:21:35,845 --> 00:21:36,972
So?

277
00:21:36,972 --> 00:21:37,806
I guess I'll see you.

278
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:39,516
We'll go ahead.

279
00:21:39,808 --> 00:21:41,434
- Already? - Right now?

280
00:21:43,270 --> 00:21:45,647
We still have our afternoon walk.

281
00:21:47,023 --> 00:21:48,649
Alright. Let’s go.

282
00:21:49,025 --> 00:21:50,026
- Bye. - Bye.

283
00:21:50,318 --> 00:21:51,778
Take care.

284
00:22:00,245 --> 00:22:00,954
Ready?

285
00:22:02,914 --> 00:22:04,124
Let's go home.

286
00:22:08,503 --> 00:22:11,506
Travel the world. Have a tour package.

287
00:22:42,495 --> 00:22:44,844
I made this in memory of Marco.

288
00:22:46,374 --> 00:22:47,459
I’m sorry.

289
00:22:50,712 --> 00:22:52,964
I’m sorry I wasn’t able to take care of you.

290
00:22:54,841 --> 00:22:56,968
That’s why you’re not with us now.

291
00:22:58,595 --> 00:23:01,348
Sorry, I wasn’t able to visit you right away.

292
00:23:04,598 --> 00:23:08,435
I just wanted your mommy to be okay when she comes back.

293
00:23:12,755 --> 00:23:14,689
Just know that I love you.

294
00:23:15,862 --> 00:23:17,946
I love you very much.

295
00:23:21,977 --> 00:23:25,469
You'll always be my Baby Marco.

296
00:23:29,667 --> 00:23:31,345
My little angel.

297
00:23:43,890 --> 00:23:47,185
Emma, that's your Daddy Drake.

298
00:23:47,185 --> 00:23:49,771
The one I showed you in the pictures.

299
00:23:49,771 --> 00:23:50,563
This one.

300
00:23:54,192 --> 00:23:55,443
Daddy!

301
00:23:57,153 --> 00:23:58,405
That's your daddy, yes!

302
00:23:58,405 --> 00:23:59,322
That's right!

303
00:24:26,599 --> 00:24:27,809
He's a good dad, you know.

304
00:24:29,644 --> 00:24:31,396
We agreed on co-parenting.

305
00:24:33,064 --> 00:24:35,358
He respected it when I asked for space.

306
00:24:35,567 --> 00:24:36,734
He never bothered us.

307
00:24:37,819 --> 00:24:40,655
But he still kept showing up in the ways he could.

308
00:24:41,698 --> 00:24:42,824
He sends her gifts.

309
00:24:43,324 --> 00:24:44,576
Checks in.

310
00:24:45,076 --> 00:24:46,703
More than enough for the child.

311
00:24:48,204 --> 00:24:52,041
So, they've never met before but they're already that close?

312
00:24:52,250 --> 00:24:53,376
Right?

313
00:24:54,586 --> 00:24:57,505
He was in the U.S. for the most part when our daughter was growing up.

314
00:24:58,173 --> 00:25:01,134
But, only from afar.

315
00:25:01,718 --> 00:25:04,095
I tested him but he still kept coming back.

316
00:25:05,138 --> 00:25:07,140
He's serious about being a father.

317
00:25:08,683 --> 00:25:11,811
I felt sorry for him because he kept on going to the U.S.,

318
00:25:11,811 --> 00:25:14,564
but I don't let him get close to our daughter.

319
00:25:15,565 --> 00:25:18,067
But, I also knew

320
00:25:18,067 --> 00:25:21,029
that he wasn't there solely for our child.

321
00:25:22,864 --> 00:25:23,698
What do you mean?

322
00:25:25,241 --> 00:25:28,995
He fought hard to stop himself from seeing you, Alys.

323
00:25:30,914 --> 00:25:33,541
He was very much aware that you needed your space.

324
00:25:34,209 --> 00:25:35,335
So, he waited.

325
00:25:35,919 --> 00:25:38,004
And lucky for him,

326
00:25:38,004 --> 00:25:40,507
by the time he couldn't help himself from going,

327
00:25:41,090 --> 00:25:42,675
you were ready to open up again.

328
00:25:43,885 --> 00:25:44,802
The proposal.

329
00:25:45,386 --> 00:25:46,804
All in good time, right?

330
00:25:47,472 --> 00:25:48,097
Yes.

331
00:25:49,224 --> 00:25:50,475
You're lucky, Alys.

332
00:25:51,559 --> 00:25:54,646
You got to see him grow at the same time his love for you did.

333
00:25:56,147 --> 00:25:58,650
And by the way, congratulations on your engagement.

334
00:25:59,359 --> 00:26:00,026
Thank you.

335
00:26:00,109 --> 00:26:01,611
Well, technically,

336
00:26:02,654 --> 00:26:03,530
re-engagement.

337
00:26:11,496 --> 00:26:12,413
They're so cute.

338
00:26:12,413 --> 00:26:13,122
Right?

339
00:26:13,540 --> 00:26:14,666
They look alike.

340
00:26:15,500 --> 00:26:16,417
- True. - Very much alike.

341
00:26:16,417 --> 00:26:17,377
She looks like you too.

342
00:26:17,377 --> 00:26:17,877
Really?

343
00:26:17,877 --> 00:26:18,169
Mhm.

344
00:26:18,878 --> 00:26:19,796
Thank you.

345
00:26:21,798 --> 00:26:23,299
What a long day.

346
00:26:39,899 --> 00:26:41,901
It's my best friend's big day tomorrow.

347
00:26:41,901 --> 00:26:43,278
It's a long time coming.

348
00:26:54,455 --> 00:26:57,917
I still got a lot to do.

349
00:26:58,626 --> 00:27:02,422
Bestie, why don't you just type those up?

350
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:06,884
Aya, she just wants it to be more personal.

351
00:27:07,927 --> 00:27:08,803
Hey!

352
00:27:09,262 --> 00:27:11,472
Are you going to fight again?

353
00:27:13,641 --> 00:27:15,518
Where are the flowers and butterflies?

354
00:27:15,518 --> 00:27:17,353
They're still not here.

355
00:27:17,770 --> 00:27:19,772
Even the guests are not complete.

356
00:27:19,772 --> 00:27:21,357
When will they be complete?

357
00:27:21,357 --> 00:27:22,483
Alys!

358
00:27:23,526 --> 00:27:24,986
Don't stress yourself.

359
00:27:25,111 --> 00:27:26,821
Everything will be fine.

360
00:27:27,322 --> 00:27:28,489
Yeah, you know what?

361
00:27:28,865 --> 00:27:30,450
Why don't you just give me that checklist?

362
00:27:30,783 --> 00:27:32,160
Kei and I will take care of it.

363
00:27:32,827 --> 00:27:33,536
Sure?

364
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:35,379
Yeah, of course.

365
00:27:37,540 --> 00:27:42,253
What's the point of having bridesmaids if you're going to do everything yourself?

366
00:27:42,712 --> 00:27:45,590
Wow, how about the maid of honor?

367
00:27:45,798 --> 00:27:46,633
You know what?

368
00:27:46,633 --> 00:27:48,009
You're so sensitive.

369
00:27:48,009 --> 00:27:49,426
Not everything's about you.

370
00:27:49,969 --> 00:27:52,055
Okay, before you guys start fighting again.

371
00:27:52,055 --> 00:27:52,889
Let’s just go, Shaira.

372
00:27:53,848 --> 00:27:54,682
What?

373
00:27:54,682 --> 00:27:55,808
I'm not starting a fight.

374
00:27:55,808 --> 00:27:57,101
I'm just concerned.

375
00:27:57,352 --> 00:27:58,353
She's pregnant.

376
00:27:58,353 --> 00:27:59,854
I don't want her to be stressed out.

377
00:28:02,774 --> 00:28:03,858
Are you guys sure?

378
00:28:03,858 --> 00:28:05,693
Sounds like you're already fighting.

379
00:28:05,818 --> 00:28:08,029
Bestie, stop micromanaging.

380
00:28:08,363 --> 00:28:10,073
Trust us, Alys.

381
00:28:10,073 --> 00:28:12,992
You're going to have the most perfect wedding ever!

382
00:28:13,493 --> 00:28:16,537
And we'll take care of the butterflies!

383
00:28:17,538 --> 00:28:18,414
Yes.

384
00:28:18,414 --> 00:28:20,124
- So, let's go? - Let’s go?

385
00:28:20,124 --> 00:28:21,000
Let's go.

386
00:28:21,250 --> 00:28:23,753
- Oh, after that we could take a dip in the pool! - Thank you, girls!

387
00:28:32,804 --> 00:28:33,773
Bestie,

388
00:28:34,972 --> 00:28:36,172
I'm sorry.

389
00:28:36,641 --> 00:28:38,226
I know I'm your maid of honor

390
00:28:38,226 --> 00:28:39,476
but it's like...

391
00:28:40,561 --> 00:28:42,021
I wasn’t much help.

392
00:28:42,355 --> 00:28:43,439
Come on, Bestie.

393
00:28:43,439 --> 00:28:45,066
Don't worry about it. It's fine!

394
00:28:46,150 --> 00:28:47,610
Bestie?

395
00:28:47,610 --> 00:28:49,529
I'm really happy for you.

396
00:28:51,072 --> 00:28:53,116
You’ve waited so long for this.

397
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:58,037
I wish this to be your happy ever after.

398
00:29:01,165 --> 00:29:02,792
What's with the face?

399
00:29:04,919 --> 00:29:05,920
Nothing.

400
00:29:07,296 --> 00:29:08,423
Bestie?

401
00:29:12,885 --> 00:29:14,011
I don't really know.

402
00:29:14,595 --> 00:29:15,930
I mean, we’re okay.

403
00:29:16,389 --> 00:29:18,057
I’m doing great. Drake and I are fine.

404
00:29:18,683 --> 00:29:19,434
But?

405
00:29:21,978 --> 00:29:23,146
But it's like...

406
00:29:24,731 --> 00:29:26,691
I’m the one who’s not sure about this.

407
00:29:29,694 --> 00:29:31,821
I don't understand myself.

408
00:29:31,821 --> 00:29:33,239
Shouldn't I be happy?

409
00:29:33,740 --> 00:29:35,992
I don't know why I'm thinking about this.

410
00:29:36,701 --> 00:29:38,161
That's normal, Bestie.

411
00:29:38,161 --> 00:29:39,495
Wedding jitters.

412
00:29:40,163 --> 00:29:42,415
It’s more than just feeling nervous.

413
00:29:45,251 --> 00:29:47,044
A lot of things will change.

414
00:29:47,879 --> 00:29:50,047
A lot of things in my life will change.

415
00:29:50,673 --> 00:29:52,759
I mean, the first time Drake and I got married,

416
00:29:52,759 --> 00:29:54,343
I didn't put in much thought.

417
00:29:54,343 --> 00:29:55,636
Then everything happened.

418
00:29:55,887 --> 00:29:57,394
Look at where it got us.

419
00:29:57,464 --> 00:29:58,470
That's true.

420
00:29:58,848 --> 00:30:01,768
And if I make this decision, there's no going back.

421
00:30:01,768 --> 00:30:03,311
Bestie, there's always a choice.

422
00:30:03,728 --> 00:30:06,329
But you wouldn't let it get to that.

423
00:30:06,981 --> 00:30:09,650
Maybe I'm just afraid that...

424
00:30:10,318 --> 00:30:11,944
I won't be enough.

425
00:30:12,862 --> 00:30:14,238
For Drake?

426
00:30:17,116 --> 00:30:18,688
Or...

427
00:30:19,644 --> 00:30:22,814
for the life that I'm getting myself into.

428
00:30:24,207 --> 00:30:27,794
Bestie, you don't have to be perfect.

429
00:30:28,711 --> 00:30:31,964
Drake isn't marrying you because you're perfect.

430
00:30:34,050 --> 00:30:37,762
He's marrying you for you.

431
00:30:40,223 --> 00:30:41,724
Thank you, Bestie.

432
00:30:43,226 --> 00:30:44,560
My maid of honor.

433
00:30:44,769 --> 00:30:45,478
Yes.

434
00:30:45,478 --> 00:30:46,813
And my godchild.

435
00:31:03,287 --> 00:31:04,580
Relax.

436
00:31:06,123 --> 00:31:07,708
You've been like this for a while.

437
00:31:08,835 --> 00:31:10,378
Are you stressed at work?

438
00:31:11,295 --> 00:31:12,296
This isn’t work.

439
00:31:13,548 --> 00:31:14,340
Then, what’s that?

440
00:31:14,340 --> 00:31:15,800
You've been on that laptop for a while.

441
00:31:16,884 --> 00:31:18,821
Yes, but not for work.

442
00:31:19,720 --> 00:31:20,513
What's that for?

443
00:31:20,513 --> 00:31:21,556
You've been there for a while.

444
00:31:24,976 --> 00:31:26,435
Hello?

445
00:31:26,978 --> 00:31:27,868
My vow.

446
00:31:29,689 --> 00:31:30,565
Your vows?

447
00:31:31,023 --> 00:31:32,233
Why are you doing your vows?

448
00:31:32,233 --> 00:31:33,985
Didn't we agree to be spontaneous?

449
00:31:34,610 --> 00:31:35,423
Because.

450
00:31:36,046 --> 00:31:38,048
Because what?

451
00:31:40,749 --> 00:31:42,710
Alys, can you stop asking questions?

452
00:31:43,411 --> 00:31:44,837
Just leave it, okay?

453
00:31:46,330 --> 00:31:48,291
And we're back with grumpy Drake again.

454
00:31:49,584 --> 00:31:50,459
Come on.

455
00:31:50,710 --> 00:31:52,587
You know how annoying I am, right?

456
00:31:52,803 --> 00:31:54,856
I'll annoy you more and more.

457
00:31:54,881 --> 00:31:56,632
Come on, what is it?

458
00:31:56,786 --> 00:31:57,984
What is it?

459
00:31:58,009 --> 00:31:59,927
What is it?

460
00:32:00,386 --> 00:32:01,110
Fine!

461
00:32:06,601 --> 00:32:09,061
I’m scared I’ll blank out on the day of the wedding.

462
00:32:10,479 --> 00:32:12,148
And I'll ruin the whole ceremony.

463
00:32:13,065 --> 00:32:13,759
Hmm?

464
00:32:18,321 --> 00:32:19,780
You? Stuttering?

465
00:32:20,031 --> 00:32:22,992
The Drake Palma I know doesn’t stutter.

466
00:32:22,992 --> 00:32:24,160
As if.

467
00:32:25,286 --> 00:32:28,789
You have no idea what you do to me, Alys.

468
00:32:31,959 --> 00:32:33,377
On the wedding day,

469
00:32:34,170 --> 00:32:36,881
seeing you with that white gown,

470
00:32:36,881 --> 00:32:38,633
and you smiling at me.

471
00:32:39,258 --> 00:32:41,302
That alone is enough to leave me speechless.

472
00:32:51,306 --> 00:32:53,475
You're madly in love with me.

473
00:32:58,819 --> 00:33:02,251
You have no idea how much I love you.

474
00:33:03,973 --> 00:33:07,415
Yes, I do have an idea how much you love me.

475
00:33:08,587 --> 00:33:10,048
To the moon and back.

476
00:33:16,545 --> 00:33:17,634
Yes, Alys.

477
00:33:22,051 --> 00:33:24,470
I'll marry you anywhere, baby.

478
00:33:26,639 --> 00:33:27,923
I mean,

479
00:33:28,391 --> 00:33:29,852
I'll marry you

480
00:33:30,726 --> 00:33:33,813
as long as you are the bride and I'm the groom.

481
00:33:36,857 --> 00:33:38,401
You deserve everything.

482
00:33:39,485 --> 00:33:40,778
The gown.

483
00:33:41,362 --> 00:33:42,780
The venue.

484
00:33:44,740 --> 00:33:46,534
And all the preparations.

485
00:33:47,910 --> 00:33:50,287
Alys, I'm willing to give you everything.

486
00:33:51,414 --> 00:33:53,833
I’ve waited so long for this day.

487
00:33:54,417 --> 00:33:56,836
And you are worth waiting for.

488
00:34:03,843 --> 00:34:04,927
I love you.

489
00:34:10,725 --> 00:34:11,976
1131.

490
00:34:12,643 --> 00:34:14,937
Always and forever.

491
00:34:20,484 --> 00:34:21,610
Forever.

492
00:34:31,951 --> 00:34:33,369
Hi, Mom.

493
00:34:34,139 --> 00:34:36,850
I'm going to remarry Alys today.

494
00:34:39,545 --> 00:34:41,213
Remember Alys?

495
00:34:42,339 --> 00:34:43,549
The noisy...

496
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:45,342
Annoying...

497
00:34:45,634 --> 00:34:46,719
Sassy...

498
00:34:46,844 --> 00:34:48,888
And a troublesome woman.

499
00:34:51,326 --> 00:34:52,808
But you know what?

500
00:34:53,984 --> 00:34:55,412
She's strong.

501
00:34:55,811 --> 00:34:57,104
Independent.

502
00:34:57,480 --> 00:34:58,439
Brave.

503
00:34:59,322 --> 00:35:01,271
And she’s not one to give up easily.

504
00:35:02,276 --> 00:35:04,779
She loves with her whole heart.

505
00:35:05,237 --> 00:35:08,532
Forgives even when it's hard.

506
00:35:10,159 --> 00:35:12,745
She puts the people she loves first.

507
00:35:14,121 --> 00:35:18,000
And she became a woman who knows exactly what she wants.

508
00:35:18,876 --> 00:35:20,294
And what she deserves.

509
00:35:22,338 --> 00:35:24,465
This time, Mom,

510
00:35:26,842 --> 00:35:29,345
I won't let her go.

511
00:35:32,556 --> 00:35:35,810
Too bad you're not here with me right now.

512
00:35:37,144 --> 00:35:40,272
So you can see how happy I am.

513
00:35:42,858 --> 00:35:44,193
I miss you, mom.

514
00:35:47,863 --> 00:35:49,156
Come in.

515
00:35:52,159 --> 00:35:52,993
Ready?

516
00:36:08,217 --> 00:36:09,969
Drake, can I go first?

517
00:36:11,220 --> 00:36:14,640
I was the one who approached you first, right?

518
00:36:16,347 --> 00:36:18,391
Do you remember that time when

519
00:36:18,894 --> 00:36:22,231
I randomly approached you and declared that

520
00:36:22,481 --> 00:36:23,816
Drake Palma!

521
00:36:24,650 --> 00:36:26,318
You're my boyfriend now!

522
00:36:29,864 --> 00:36:34,702
I didn’t do it because I liked you or loved you.

523
00:36:34,869 --> 00:36:36,954
I did it

524
00:36:37,746 --> 00:36:39,915
for the person I loved during that time.

525
00:36:40,499 --> 00:36:42,459
And I think you know that.

526
00:36:56,015 --> 00:36:56,891
Yes.

527
00:36:58,100 --> 00:37:00,102
You were the one who approached first.

528
00:37:00,311 --> 00:37:01,353
I'm Alys!

529
00:37:01,353 --> 00:37:04,440
Alys Zyril Perez, soon to be Palma.

530
00:37:04,565 --> 00:37:05,524
Hello!

531
00:37:06,275 --> 00:37:09,612
But it just means that you were the brave one.

532
00:37:11,299 --> 00:37:14,302
You’ve always been the braver one between the two of us.

533
00:37:29,548 --> 00:37:33,010
I thought that challenge would be easy.

534
00:37:33,135 --> 00:37:34,803
But you...

535
00:37:35,971 --> 00:37:38,098
You were the difficult one, Drake.

536
00:37:39,016 --> 00:37:40,226
You were cold.

537
00:37:40,643 --> 00:37:41,685
Quiet.

538
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:42,719
Grumpy.

539
00:37:43,229 --> 00:37:43,979
What?

540
00:37:45,564 --> 00:37:48,108
You were very hard to read, Drake.

541
00:37:48,609 --> 00:37:49,568
In your dreams.

542
00:37:49,568 --> 00:37:50,736
You're ugly.

543
00:37:51,820 --> 00:37:53,322
Very unpredictable.

544
00:38:07,061 --> 00:38:08,980
We’re here now, Alys.

545
00:38:09,630 --> 00:38:12,675
I never thought we’d make it this far.

546
00:38:14,176 --> 00:38:15,511
Bird brain.

547
00:38:17,263 --> 00:38:18,222
You’re harsh!

548
00:38:18,555 --> 00:38:19,306
Noob!

549
00:38:20,516 --> 00:38:21,475
My noob!

550
00:38:22,351 --> 00:38:25,896
I never thought someone like you would accept me.

551
00:38:26,689 --> 00:38:27,898
You're annoying.

552
00:38:29,984 --> 00:38:30,943
But that's fine.

553
00:38:32,987 --> 00:38:35,364
But through it all,

554
00:38:36,198 --> 00:38:37,950
I knew you.

555
00:38:38,284 --> 00:38:39,410
All of you.

556
00:38:48,877 --> 00:38:51,422
In the midst of all my fears,

557
00:38:52,423 --> 00:38:54,800
all the fights,

558
00:38:55,097 --> 00:38:56,378
and goodbyes...

559
00:38:58,147 --> 00:39:00,024
You became my constant.

560
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:27,476
I got to know the real you.

561
00:39:29,641 --> 00:39:31,812
Not the man you show to others,

562
00:39:33,464 --> 00:39:36,383
but the man you are when no one is watching.

563
00:39:37,092 --> 00:39:37,985
Drake?!

564
00:39:38,010 --> 00:39:38,816
Shh!

565
00:39:39,803 --> 00:39:41,847
The quiet ways you care,

566
00:39:42,806 --> 00:39:44,725
the words you rarely utter,

567
00:39:44,725 --> 00:39:46,101
but cut deep.

568
00:39:47,019 --> 00:39:48,228
I'm territorial.

569
00:39:48,562 --> 00:39:49,646
I'm territorial.

570
00:39:51,231 --> 00:39:53,067
Every imperfection.

571
00:39:54,485 --> 00:39:56,028
Every side.

572
00:39:56,487 --> 00:39:58,781
The happy ones.

573
00:39:59,740 --> 00:40:00,199
Wait!

574
00:40:00,199 --> 00:40:01,367
That’s too much!

575
00:40:01,825 --> 00:40:03,744
The annoying ones.

576
00:40:05,204 --> 00:40:06,747
What's with the skimpy attire?

577
00:40:09,083 --> 00:40:10,000
Pardon me?

578
00:40:10,084 --> 00:40:13,629
The sides that I'm scared of.

579
00:40:13,921 --> 00:40:15,672
Alys, what do you mean what's my deal?

580
00:40:17,007 --> 00:40:20,344
The sides that are so hard to understand.

581
00:40:22,054 --> 00:40:23,138
Where are we going?

582
00:40:24,556 --> 00:40:25,682
What do you mean?

583
00:40:25,682 --> 00:40:26,892
Why are you here?

584
00:40:26,975 --> 00:40:27,927
Feeling close?

585
00:40:27,952 --> 00:40:28,888
Are we close?

586
00:40:30,229 --> 00:40:31,105
Alys...

587
00:40:31,355 --> 00:40:32,773
We were pretty close.

588
00:40:33,440 --> 00:40:34,858
We were exes, remember?

589
00:40:35,442 --> 00:40:36,527
We used to hug.

590
00:40:37,277 --> 00:40:38,028
We used to —

591
00:40:38,028 --> 00:40:39,363
What do you want, Drake?

592
00:40:39,613 --> 00:40:41,198
We hurt each other.

593
00:40:42,074 --> 00:40:43,033
We broke up.

594
00:40:43,867 --> 00:40:45,452
We got tired so many times.

595
00:40:46,078 --> 00:40:47,121
We gave up.

596
00:40:49,915 --> 00:40:51,118
Drake!

597
00:40:51,542 --> 00:40:53,419
You will regret this, Drake Palma!

598
00:40:53,419 --> 00:40:57,005
Drink and forget.

599
00:40:57,005 --> 00:40:58,632
Drink until you forget.

600
00:40:59,425 --> 00:41:02,428
After all the fights we’ve been through,

601
00:41:02,428 --> 00:41:04,471
settled on,

602
00:41:07,224 --> 00:41:09,268
and everything we’ve been through.

603
00:41:10,769 --> 00:41:12,521
Drake,

604
00:41:12,980 --> 00:41:14,565
if you love me,

605
00:41:16,442 --> 00:41:18,152
please stop this.

606
00:41:18,902 --> 00:41:20,320
Please.

607
00:41:20,988 --> 00:41:22,656
Let me go.

608
00:41:24,283 --> 00:41:26,285
We should let go of each other.

609
00:41:27,286 --> 00:41:31,165
But we found our way back to each other.

610
00:41:32,499 --> 00:41:34,001
Damn you, Palma!

611
00:41:41,842 --> 00:41:42,342
Yeah.

612
00:41:43,552 --> 00:41:44,561
Damn me.

613
00:41:47,509 --> 00:41:50,053
Even after being apart for so long,

614
00:41:51,351 --> 00:41:53,937
there’s one thing that never changed.

615
00:41:56,064 --> 00:41:58,650
And that's my love for you, Drake.

616
00:42:00,110 --> 00:42:02,070
I love you so much, Alys.

617
00:42:03,780 --> 00:42:07,493
I can’t promise you that we’ll never face challenges again.

618
00:42:08,785 --> 00:42:10,746
But I promise you,

619
00:42:10,746 --> 00:42:14,166
no matter what challenges we face, I’ll never leave your side.

620
00:42:15,375 --> 00:42:18,128
On the easy days,

621
00:42:18,629 --> 00:42:21,840
and especially the hard ones.

622
00:42:23,091 --> 00:42:26,929
On the days we’re certain,

623
00:42:27,721 --> 00:42:29,890
and the days we’re not.

624
00:42:32,476 --> 00:42:35,062
I know we had a rocky start,

625
00:42:36,313 --> 00:42:38,482
but I'm sure

626
00:42:39,566 --> 00:42:42,736
that God destined you to be with me.

627
00:42:43,570 --> 00:42:45,697
We're here now, Alys.

628
00:42:46,657 --> 00:42:48,408
One thing is certain.

629
00:42:51,245 --> 00:42:54,581
I can't live without you by my side, my noob.

630
00:42:56,124 --> 00:42:59,044
There's only one thing

631
00:42:59,836 --> 00:43:01,412
I can promise you.

632
00:43:03,298 --> 00:43:07,386
I will always, always choose you.

633
00:43:08,428 --> 00:43:12,099
Because I always find my way back home to you.

634
00:43:13,684 --> 00:43:15,769
Through it all, Drake...

635
00:43:15,769 --> 00:43:17,854
my Drakey baby,

636
00:43:18,438 --> 00:43:21,567
I'll always be your noob,

637
00:43:21,984 --> 00:43:24,152
your bird brain,

638
00:43:24,486 --> 00:43:30,117
your little Alys who loves you very, very, very much, Drake.

639
00:43:30,701 --> 00:43:33,453
To the moon and back.

640
00:43:34,037 --> 00:43:35,831
Just as you promised me,

641
00:43:37,833 --> 00:43:39,585
I will always

642
00:43:40,210 --> 00:43:43,255
love you to the moon and back, Alys Zyril Perez.

643
00:43:44,423 --> 00:43:45,882
I love you,

644
00:43:45,882 --> 00:43:50,387
Drake Sebastian Jimenez Palma.

645
00:43:51,430 --> 00:43:54,933
I'm the luckiest man in the world.

646
00:43:55,475 --> 00:43:57,519
Because I have you.

647
00:44:02,482 --> 00:44:03,734
I love you.

648
00:44:05,319 --> 00:44:06,403
My noob.

649
00:45:36,827 --> 00:45:38,745
Alys,

650
00:45:39,454 --> 00:45:40,997
take this ring

651
00:45:41,915 --> 00:45:43,500
as a symbol of my love,

652
00:45:44,543 --> 00:45:45,961
commitment

653
00:45:46,378 --> 00:45:48,839
and the promise of all my tomorrows.

654
00:45:59,015 --> 00:46:00,642
Drake,

655
00:46:01,476 --> 00:46:03,145
take this ring

656
00:46:03,437 --> 00:46:06,106
as a symbol of all my love and vows

657
00:46:07,065 --> 00:46:09,651
for all that I am and all that I have.

658
00:46:10,277 --> 00:46:11,319
I honor you.

659
00:46:16,032 --> 00:46:19,161
By the power vested in me, I pronounce you

660
00:46:19,161 --> 00:46:20,328
husband and wife.

661
00:46:20,996 --> 00:46:22,289
You may now kiss the bride.

662
00:46:32,799 --> 00:46:33,675
Oh!

663
00:46:33,675 --> 00:46:35,635
Drake, be careful.

664
00:47:40,176 --> 00:47:44,013
From dating Alys Perez to marrying Alys Perez...

665
00:47:44,329 --> 00:47:45,205
Done!

666
00:47:46,039 --> 00:47:47,791
Seducing Drake Palma...

667
00:47:48,166 --> 00:47:50,001
Mission accomplished!

668
00:48:38,633 --> 00:48:40,468
3, 2, 1...

669
00:48:41,289 --> 00:48:42,165
Action!

670
00:48:42,436 --> 00:48:43,270
Good morning!

671
00:48:45,181 --> 00:48:46,391
Go in!

672
00:48:46,391 --> 00:48:51,313
Dana and Andy did a great job on the papers and essay.

673
00:48:51,338 --> 00:48:53,924
Alys and Andy did a great job on the papers...

674
00:48:54,357 --> 00:48:55,483
and the essay —

675
00:49:02,282 --> 00:49:05,243
Alys, Tripp still has a line.

676
00:49:11,541 --> 00:49:13,710
Distance makes the heart grow...

677
00:49:14,502 --> 00:49:15,629
...stronger?

678
00:49:29,851 --> 00:49:31,061
You stand noisily!

679
00:49:40,403 --> 00:49:42,322
She already knows how to drive!

680
00:49:53,153 --> 00:49:55,655
Let’s give Rabin a round of applause!

681
00:49:56,211 --> 00:49:59,422
[singing] And if we make it to the end...

682
00:49:59,422 --> 00:50:00,382
The book already closed!

683
00:50:06,903 --> 00:50:08,981
Sheen is getting all flustered.

684
00:50:09,106 --> 00:50:10,266
Get out!

685
00:50:10,328 --> 00:50:11,661
Is that right?

686
00:50:12,102 --> 00:50:12,936
Third wheel!

687
00:50:12,991 --> 00:50:14,551
My nose is bleeding.

688
00:50:47,637 --> 00:50:49,681
[singing]

689
00:50:50,882 --> 00:50:52,050
Are you crying?

690
00:50:52,308 --> 00:50:54,602
Oh, I don’t have a teaser of the next episode!

691
00:50:55,854 --> 00:50:57,439
It's a wrap!

692
00:51:00,859 --> 00:51:02,610
Thank you, guys!

693
00:51:02,610 --> 00:51:05,030
Thank you, DAP Team. It’s a wrap.
